.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt NVRM 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvrm
.Nd model of the libnvrm device description and memory rules
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr nvrm 3
describes a GPU in layers.
Every device starts as an abstract device; each layer fills or overrides only
what it knows, and the rest stays unavailable with a reason.
Consumers use the abstract and class members only.
.Bl -tag -width "board decorators"
.It abstract device
Identity: PCI location and identifiers, subsystem identifiers, RM GPU id, UUID.
.It class
What any compute or graphics GPU reports: architecture, implementation, chip
id, raw RM SM version and compute capability, GPC, TPC and SM counts, the class
list, memory sizes, page sizes and the capability flags.
.It family
Values only a generation table knows, selected by the pair of GPFIFO and
compute classes the GPU lists: family name, the channel, compute, 3D and copy
classes and the page size candidates.
A GPU the table does not know is still described; the family values are then
unavailable with the reason
.Li family_unknown .
The library core names no chip.
.It board decorators
Entries keyed by PCI subsystem identifiers that only add or override options.
A decorator never decides whether a GPU is supported.
None exists yet: none is added without a real board that needs it.
.El
.Ss Availability
Every value is available, or carries a reason identifier and a source:
.Li rm ,
.Li os ,
.Li derived ,
.Li family
or
.Li board .
An unavailable value is never reported as a number.
VRAM size 0 on a unified-memory part is available, with the value 0.
.Ss SM and compute versions
.Li sm_version_major
and
.Li sm_version_minor
are the RM's numbering, formed by splitting the raw RM code at its high and low
bytes; they are not necessarily CUDA compute capability numbers.
.Li rm_sm_version
preserves that raw code.
.Li compute_capability_major
and
.Li compute_capability_minor
are derived only from the architecture/implementation table.
When that table has no row, both are unavailable with reason
.Li family_unknown :
neither an RM alias nor the raw high and low bytes is a compute capability.
The reason does not depend on the raw code: zero or an unavailable raw code
without a table row is
.Li family_unknown
too.
Only a missing architecture or implementation leaves compute capability
unavailable with reason
.Li input_unavailable .
The raw code remains available separately as
.Li rm_sm_version
when the RM reports it.
For example, GB206 reports raw RM SM 10.4 but has compute capability 12.0;
GB20B has compute capability 12.1.
.Ss Reasons
The reason identifiers of an unavailable value:
.Bl -tag -width "family_has_no_class" -compact
.It Li not_queried
the value was not queried.
.It Li rm_control_failed
the RM control returned an error.
.It Li rm_not_supported
the RM reports the control is not supported on this GPU.
.It Li os_not_reported
the OS layer does not report the value.
.It Li family_unknown
the GPU matched no row of the generation table (the family is unknown).
.It Li family_has_no_class
the family is known and has no class of this kind.
.It Li input_unavailable
a value this one is computed from is unavailable.
.It Li no_numa_node
the GPU is not attached to a NUMA node.
.It Li backend_does_not_provide
the backend does not provide the value.
.It Li class_absent
the GPU does not list the class.
.It Li os_call_failed
the system call to the driver failed.
.It Li value_unusable
the RM answered, but the answer failed a consistency check (it names another
device, or exceeds what the library can count).
.It Li version_unparsed
a version string has no readable numeric scheme or exceeds the parser bounds.
.It Li version_inconsistent
the kernel module version sysctls disagree with its version string.
.El
.Ss Capabilities
A fixed, indexed set of flags; the index is stable and new flags are only
appended.
Each is available (yes or no) or carries a reason.
.Bl -tag -width "0 coherent_gpu_memory" -compact
.It 0 Li dmabuf_export
the RM can export memory as a dma-buf (GPU info index DMABUF_CAPABILITY).
.It 1 Li ats
address translation services (GPU_ATS_CAPABILITY).
.It 2 Li self_hosted
the GPU is self-hosted (GPU_SELF_HOSTED_CAPABILITY).
.It 3 Li display_enabled
the GPU has an enabled display engine (DISPLAY_ENABLED).
.It 4 Li soc
the GPU is part of a system on a chip (the SOC bit of the GPU id flags).
.It 5 Li coherent_gpu_memory
GPU memory is CPU coherent (COHERENT_GPU_MEMORY_MODE is not NONE).
.It 6 Li os_device_wc_active
the OS layer maps device memory write-combined on this host: the sysctl
.Va hw.nvidia.altra_device_wc_active ,
the Ampere Altra memory attribute decision.
.El
.Ss Backends
.Bl -tag -width "fake"
.It rm
The NVIDIA kernel module, through the RM escape ioctls.
The RM version of the module must equal the version
.Xr nvrm 3
was built for; otherwise it refuses to run and says which version it found.
.It fake
Synthetic data for tests and for machines without a GPU.
.El
.Ss Capsicum
The default is least privilege.
After enumeration the descriptors are limited to the ioctl and event rights
and to the RM escapes control and free: enough to read device information and
to release it, with no allocation.
A caller that will allocate RM objects after
.Xr cap_enter 2
sets
.Dv NVRM_ENUM_ALLOW_ALLOC
in the enumeration option flags; the descriptors then also keep the allocate
escape.
The enumeration descriptors never carry a mapping right, in either case.
It must say so before the limit is applied, because Capsicum rights can only be
narrowed, never widened.
Memory is mapped through a client of its own
.Pq Xr nvrm_mem 3 :
only a client opened with
.Dv NVRM_OPEN_ALLOW_MAP
holds descriptors with the right to be mapped, opened and limited before
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
one for each CPU mapping it can make there.
.Xr nvrm-info 8
uses the default.
After enumeration the process may call
.Xr cap_enter 2
and keep calling
.Fn nvrm_device_refresh .
OS-layer values (sysctl, card list) are read before and kept.
.Ss Memory attributes
The attribute a CPU mapping of GPU memory gets, as
.Xr nvrm_mem 3
reports it in
.Va cpu_attr :
.Bl -tag -width "video memory, arm64"
.It system memory
Write-back
.Pq Dv NVRM_ATTR_CACHED ,
unless its owner made it otherwise: an imported object the RM keeps
write-combined is
.Dv NVRM_ATTR_WC ,
and one it keeps uncached, write-through or write-protected follows the
Device rule on every host.
.It video memory, not arm64
A PCIe BAR, write-combined
.Pq Dv NVRM_ATTR_WC .
.It video memory, arm64
.Dv NVRM_ATTR_WC
(Normal non-cacheable) when the capability
.Li os_device_wc_active
is 0;
.Dv NVRM_ATTR_DEVICE
(Device-nGnRE) when it is 1, because the OS layer then falls back to
Device memory for write-combining, or when it is not reported.
.El
.Pp
Through Device memory only aligned accesses of 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes are safe;
an unaligned access, or a copy routine that makes one, can fault.
A GPU with no video memory of its own (VRAM size 0) places video memory
allocations in system memory.
.Ss Channels
.Xr nvrm_chan 3
submits ordered GPFIFO work, reports progress through a semaphore, and isolates
a dead channel from the other channels of its client.
.Ss JSON
Schema
.Li nvrm-info/1 ,
minor 3;
documents name it in the
.Li schema
member.
Document and header records have a
.Li versions
object whose members preserve each version string and, when available, expose
its integer parts and source.
The object covers the running driver, RM API, built-for RM, library, library
symbols and schema versions.
Additive changes raise the minor number; a breaking change is a new major
schema installed beside the old one.
The identifiers (reason ids, error codes, source names and the capability
index and name pairs) are frozen in
.Pa lib/libnvrm/schema/nvrm-info-1.ids ;
the test suite compares the schema with that baseline and refuses one that
removes, renames or renumbers an identifier.
Minor 1 added the error codes of the memory calls.
Minor 2 added the versions object, the version fields of a device and the
reasons
.Dq version_unparsed
and
.Dq version_inconsistent .
Minor 3 added the channel error codes
.Dq timeout
and
.Dq channel_lost .
Until the first package release the interface is provisional (see
.Xr nvrm 3 ) ,
and this schema is minor 3 of it.
.Sh SEE ALSO
